{
 "artist": "Albert Bierstadt",
 "slug": "albert-bierstadt",
 "born": 1830,
 "died": 1902,
 "nationality": "American (born in Germany)",
 "facts": [
  {
   "text": "Bierstadt's usual signature joins his initials into a monogram, so that 'AB' runs straight into the surname: museums record it as 'ABierstadt' with the AB in monogram.",
   "source": "https://www.clevelandart.org/art/1922.684",
   "source_name": "Cleveland Museum of Art"
  },
  {
   "text": "He often added a two-digit year under or after the signature, as in 'ABierstadt. / 66' on Mount Starr King, Yosemite (1866) and 'ABierstadt./64.' on Valley of the Yosemite.",
   "source": "https://www.clevelandart.org/art/1922.684",
   "source_name": "Cleveland Museum of Art"
  },
  {
   "text": "His earliest painting at the National Gallery of Art, Lake Lucerne (1858), is already signed 'ABierstadt. / 1858.' at lower right.",
   "source": "https://www.nga.gov/collection/art-object-page.71503.html",
   "source_name": "National Gallery of Art"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Last of the Buffalo (1888–89) is signed in full, 'Albert Bierstadt'; a photogravure of it was copyrighted by Bierstadt in 1891, and the National Gallery's impression is inscribed in pencil 'Senator Sherman / with Compliments of / Albert Bierstadt'.",
   "source": "https://www.nga.gov/collection/art-object-page.172895.html",
   "source_name": "National Gallery of Art"
  },
  {
   "text": "Catalogues record the monogrammed signature at lower left on some works and lower right on others; on Mt. Baker, Washington (1890) it is at lower left.",
   "source": "https://www.brooklynmuseum.org/objects/962",
   "source_name": "Brooklyn Museum"
  }
 ],
